	"img": "systems/a5e/assets/Lesser_Mask_of_the_Desert_Nomad.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>This mask is made to look almost exactly like a @UUID[Compendium.a5e-dastardly-desert-deeds.equipment.Item.oY0pmlI71wATgRBY]{Mask of the Desert Nomad}, but is much more common. It does not grant all the same protections as the real one, but it does afford partial protection against sunburn –it will take twice the amount of time for the wearer to get sunburn than it would take without.</p><p>Bazaar owners and merchants sell these masks to tourists and travelers, often peddling them as the real thing. A DC 18 Culture check can notice the subtle difference in the lighter color of the clay and duller sheen of the golden cracks.</p>",
